    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following. $\\dfrac{3x}{x-2}-\\dfrac6{x+2}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3(x^2+4)}{x^2-4}$, $x\\ne-2,2$.\n\nUse the common denominator $(x-2)(x+2)$.",
      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne-2,2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3x}{x-2}-\\frac6{x+2}&=\\frac{3x(x+2)-6(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3x}{x-2}-\\frac6{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2+6x-6x+12}{x^2-4}\\\\\\frac{3x}{x-2}-\\frac6{x+2}&=\\frac{3(x^2+4)}{x^2-4}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
  },
